I know that the cube root of a number is the same as raising that number to the power of 1/3. So, maybe I can rewrite all these roots as exponents with base 10 or something? Wait, actually, since we are dealing with exponents and roots, maybe it's better to express everything in terms of exponents with the same base or something?

Alternatively, maybe I can combine the two cube roots first before dealing with the inverse? Let me see.

